Author: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 18 08:42:32 2026 +1100

    Stop relying on the $stream dnf variable for the NFV repo.
    
    The centos-nfv-openvswitch metalink was built from $stream, which
    dnf only expands when /etc/dnf/vars/stream exists. Rocky Linux 10.2's
    rocky-repos package shipped that file (stream=10-stream); 10.3's does
    not, and quay.io/rockylinux/rockylinux:10 now points at 10.3. dnf
    therefore sends a literal "$stream" to mirrors.centos.org, which
    answers 404, and every image that installs openvswitch
    (openvswitch-base, kolla-toolbox, nova-libvirt) fails to build:
    
      Error: Failed to download metadata for repo 'centos-nfv-openvswitch':
      Cannot prepare internal mirrorlist: Status code: 404 for
      https://mirrors.centos.org/metalink?repo=centos-nfv-sig-openvswitch-2-$stream&...
    
    Build the stream name from $releasever_major instead, which dnf
    always defines. On Rocky 10 it expands to 10-stream, the value the
    variable used to hold, and openvswitch3.5 resolves from the repo
    again.
    
    Prompt: Michael asked for the Rocky 10 master image build failure
    blocking the kerbside-patches merge queue to be fixed.
    
    Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5

